# Ordered SoC XNU patch series for MSM8996.
# One path per line, relative to the SoC repository; blank lines and lines
# starting with '#' are ignored. An empty series is valid.
#
# 0001: SMP / dual-cluster bring-up for Kryo 280 (4 CPUs, 2 clusters).
#       Adapted from sm8550 native-smp-secondary.patch: MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS 1->2
#       and start.s MPIDR Affinity1 path. Required before secondary CPUs boot.
0001-msm8996-smp.patch
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resolved by source review (2026-11-07) — these are NOT patches: there is no
# XNU core code gap to fix. Do not author empty diffs for them.
#
#   gic-v3-3cell  XNU's IODTMapOneInterrupt parses interrupt specifiers using
#                 the controller's #interrupt-cells at runtime; ArmCpu does
#                 not read node "interrupts" at all (PSCI + direct GIC MMIO).
#                 Three-cell GICv3 specifiers need no code change. The only
#                 open question is real-hardware SMP bring-up of cpu1..cpu3,
#                 which is a DTS/observation task, not a patch.
#   smmu-v2       ArmSmmu4K already targets arm,mmu-500, i.e. SMMUv2. There
#                 is no "v2 quirk branch" to add. The real gap is an owning
#                 IOService plus clock/context-bank initialisation, which
#                 belongs in a component and requires device observation.
#
# The other three items are likewise NOT XNU core diffs. NativeUfs8996,
# Blsp8996, Adreno530 and Msm8996Platform are registered in components.toml
# and the three drivers are force-loaded into kernel.macho via
# CONFIG_XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES. Their hardware bindings are enabled in
# UniXNU-g0245d/dts/g0245d.dts (status = "okay" on &ufshc, &gpu,
# &blsp2_i2c6), because devicetree.py only exports enabled nodes to the ADT.
#
# What remains for these three is real-hardware qualification only:
#   msm8996-blsp     QUP v2 clock/reset + FIFO/block-mode I2C transactions.
#   msm8996-ufs2     HCE/HCS, UIC DME_LINKSTARTUP, UTRL/UTMRL, NOP-OUT,
#                    unit descriptors, IOBlockStorageDevice.
#   msm8996-mdp5     MDP5/DSI0 rails, PHY 28nm init, ft8716 panel timings and
#                    scanout. Blocked offline: the mdss node has no "ranges"
#                    property, so its 1-cell children cannot be exported to
#                    the ADT until the bus description is fixed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
